"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkdocs_that_speak=globalThis.webpackChunkdocs_that_speak||[]).push([[114],{5014(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"welcome","metadata":{"permalink":"/DocsThatSpeak/blog/welcome","editUrl":"https://github.com/JKwrites-tech/DocsThatSpeak/edit/main/blog/blog/welcome.mdx","source":"@site/blog/welcome.mdx","title":"Welcome Note from the Author","description":"Hello, my name is Jyoti. Welcome to Docs That Speak.","date":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"readingTime":2.34,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Jyoti Kiran","title":"Senior Technical Writer & Content Designer","socials":{},"key":null,"page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome","title":"Welcome Note from the Author","date":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","authors":[{"name":"Jyoti Kiran","title":"Senior Technical Writer & Content Designer"}]},"unlisted":false},"content":"Hello, my name is Jyoti. Welcome to Docs That Speak.\\r\\n\\r\\nI am a Senior Technical Writer and Content Designer with over eight years of experience across enterprise SaaS, cloud platforms, fintech, AI automation, banking, and industrial machinery. I have built documentation ecosystems from scratch, scaled documentation teams, and delivered content that moved real business metrics \u2014 not just page views.\\r\\n\\r\\nI have worked across the full spectrum of the craft: DITA-based structured authoring at SAP, docs-as-code pipelines at Jiffy.AI, API documentation, UX writing, content strategy, and AI-assisted workflows. The throughline in all of it is the same: documentation should serve the person reading it, not the person who wrote it.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## What you will find here?\\r\\n\\r\\nDocs That Speak is where I write about the two things:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Documentation Strategy** \u2014 how documentation functions as a business driver, not a deliverable. Measuring impact, building feedback loops, reducing support overhead, and making the case for docs at the leadership table.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is for writers who want to think bigger than the article in front of them. How do you prove your documentation is working? How do you build feedback loops that actually tell you something? How do you turn a support queue into a content roadmap? These are the questions that separate writers who deliver content from writers who drive outcomes.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Next-Gen Docs** \u2014 how the profession is evolving. AI in the documentation workflow, writing for how people actually read, and the information architecture decisions that determine whether content gets found or ignored.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEverything I write here is grounded in something that actually happened \u2014 a product I documented, a team I led, a metric that moved, a mistake I made\\r\\nand figured out how to fix.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why \\"Docs That Speak\\"?\\r\\n\\r\\nMost documentation is written to exist \u2014 to cover a feature, close a ticket, satisfy a release checklist. It sits on a help portal and waits to be found. It answers the question that was easiest\\r\\nto answer, not the question that was hardest to ask.\\r\\n\\r\\nDocumentation that speaks does something different. It meets the reader where they are, answers the question they actually have, and leaves them more capable than when they arrived. It anticipates confusion before\\r\\nit becomes a support ticket. It earns trust by being right, consistently,\\r\\nevery time.\\r\\n\\r\\nI have spent eight years learning how to meet it\\r\\nacross SAP, FIS Global, Jiffy.AI, Finastra, Epiroc, and Wipro \u2014 across\\r\\nenterprise procurement networks, banking platforms, AI automation tools,\\r\\nand heavy mining machinery. The industries were wildly different. The\\r\\nstandard never changed.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis site is where I break it down \u2014 so you can build it right.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\u270d\ufe0f Thanks for stopping by. Browse [Documentation Strategy](/docs/strategy/intro) or [Next-Gen Docs](/docs/nextgen/intro), and feel free to connect with me on [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/jyoti-kiran-a48523116).\\r\\n\\r\\n\u2014 Jyoti"}]}}')}}]);